        "end_line": null,
        "start_column": 11
      },
      "finding": "subprocess.run(command, shell=True",
      "explanation": "The `subprocess.run` function call with `shell=True` allows tool parameter abuse, which can potentially lead to shell injection. An attacker could manipulate command inputs to execute arbitrary commands, compromising the system or leaking sensitive information.",
      "remediation": "Avoid using `shell=True` and instead pass the command as a list of arguments. Sanitize or validate command inputs to ensure they are safe. Never pass untrusted data to the `run` function directly.",
      "code_snippet": "import subprocess\nimport sys\n\n\ndef run(command):\n    return subprocess.run(command, shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(run(\" \".join(sys.argv[1:])))",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Tool Misuse"
      ],
      "evidence": {
