      },
      "finding": "subprocess.run(command, shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True)",
      "explanation": "The use of the `shell=True` parameter in the `subprocess.run` function call is a security risk. This parameter allows the command to be processed through the shell, which can lead to shell injection attacks. An attacker could insert malicious shell commands, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution on the system.",
      "remediation": "Avoid using `shell=True` whenever possible. Instead, use the `args` parameter to pass the command as a list of strings. This can help prevent shell injection attacks. Ensure that any command arguments are properly sanitized or validated before passing them to the subprocess function.",
      "code_snippet": "\n\ndef run(command):\n    return subprocess.run(command, shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":",
      "intent": null,
